  "term": "coefficient of variation",
  "definition": "The coefficient of variation is a standardized measure of how much data vary relative to their average, calculated as the standard deviation divided by the mean. Because it expresses variability in a unit-free way, it helps compare the spread or uncertainty of datasets measured on different scales.",
